### Index
GET {{baseUri}}/customers HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Store
POST {{baseUri}}/customers HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "name": "Cliente Teste",
    "email": "cliente.teste@example.com",
    "phone": "44999998888",
    "birth_date": "1995-05-20"
}

### Show
# 1 é o id do cliente neste exemplo.
# Utilize um id existente em sua base de dados.
GET {{baseUri}}/customers/2 HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Update
# 1 é o id do cliente neste exemplo.
# Utilize um id existente em sua base de dados.
PUT {{baseUri}}/customers/2 HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "name": "Cliente ATUALIZADO via API/REST",
    "email": "cliente.atualizado@example.com",
    "phone": "44988887777",
    "birth_date": "1990-01-01"
}

### Delete
# Use o id do cliente criado no Store (não use 1, que já existe).
DELETE {{baseUri}}/customers/2 HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}